andard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-164171/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "7cfc870e-38df-59be-a12c-3a6faeea4378" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164171/selection/4a239361d17819febe8cdc376aa613dba0d678982000b1508f9208361635624f" :answer/id #uuid "97ff0b2e-5a45-56b3-84b0-4baebb68ba85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "217" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164171/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "00f1a4c9-2d3b-5c68-a94b-95d902cb1bf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164171/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "9b395d7d-4dda-5ac5-9bdb-e9522f8151af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164171/selection/1ba659a1785c94b0bb90e8d19f48e5ebb8e3a87bfd6b477ad1061ed143f66acd" :answer/id #uuid "bf17624b-ee25-5fa7-8b49-cc1b53d8f418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "279" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164171/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc4cb3b-efc5-5585-a82a-0e0fd4ee886f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164171/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer-field/choices ["q-164171/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-164171/selection/4a239361d17819febe8cdc376aa613dba0d678982000b1508f9208361635624f" "q-164171/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" "q-164171/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" "q-164171/selection/1ba659a1785c94b0bb90e8d19f48e5ebb8e3a87bfd6b477ad1061ed143f66acd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164171" :question/id #uuid "7753e17b-6f63-5dc9-9be9-230d0731e05e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164171" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/78c28583961f2588c3e080d227e2e4f20a557ed77dcb20a6332092fe5915b22c.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot (1+2)=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=5\\cdot 7-3\\cdot 9=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,8\\,|\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164171/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164171"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316595/field-1/de4adedcb4f94c847122905ee3a7a3f16eecda2d4ce5fbbb83bc1b08e3c95a70" :answer/id #uuid "c04ab0ea-f1d2-59b3-9018-ea51dce54821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316595/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "90209ccf-01c5-5b73-8ebd-0624635d0ae4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316595/field-1/de4adedcb4f94c847122905ee3a7a3f16eecda2d4ce5fbbb83bc1b08e3c95a70" :answer-field/choices ["q-316595/field-1/de4adedcb4f94c847122905ee3a7a3f16eecda2d4ce5fbbb83bc1b08e3c95a70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316595" :question/id #uuid "94ee92da-e759-5ee5-a9ca-480d05dc9adb" :question/math-academy-id "q-316595" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/54537b6712dc9ae74b8b65cd0a14d5d3e878709ae35b2fc5701c7b1a6dd6d044.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(5+2)\\cdot 2=7.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-3)\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 0=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-9\\,|\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316595/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-12282"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/fa0dbfe03050a0ca52f2fbe1988a9e6475cd24437c619dba27a4fed984736fc1.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-316588"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/cec4f46a70e55735e07cc77fb2013c8d5262ca15feda1ee9eac005a79d38147d.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-316612"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/92ee29a22baa10f4af25db8221e7d67c729f5f0f1b5e1b3c37aee7e31a92bdfb.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-3)=4+3=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-9296/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6be72b2f-e1f7-518b-9c1f-e027bdc503f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9296/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "eba9837d-5e82-5a94-9370-80b6105b5754" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" 